1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,387
QuakeSense asks when local AI leadership improves earthquake evacuation. This public demo connects inspectable micro mechanisms, seven overseas city simulations, and measured AMD Radeon plus ROCm execution.

2
00:00:15,937 --> 00:00:30,104
The system closes a full loop. Leaders observe road access, shelter pressure, and resident belief, reason with a local model, call validated tools, and write decisions back into the resident simulation.

3
00:00:30,654 --> 00:00:46,155
At the microscopic level, roles matter. Commanders broadcast, informed residents guide, uninformed residents follow, volunteers assist elderly people and children, and responders manage arrivals at shelters.

4
00:00:46,705 --> 00:01:03,137
Four implemented rules create the city process. Departure delays are distributed, boundary flow is limited by width and pedestrian specific flow, destinations require remaining shelter capacity, and every time step conserves population.

5
00:01:03,687 --> 00:01:16,874
Los Angeles is the large metropolitan case. The animation shows in-transit density, cumulative shelter arrivals, and the remaining population changing across the full simulated horizon.

6
00:01:17,424 --> 00:01:30,461
Naples shows how dense urban structure can support access while still producing local queues. Orange marks movement, green marks shelter arrivals, and white points show candidate destinations.

7
00:01:31,011 --> 00:01:42,988
Wellington provides a compact high-access case. The same playback format makes the time path directly comparable with every other city instead of selecting one favorable static snapshot.

8
00:01:43,538 --> 00:01:56,500
L Aquila illustrates a smaller, lower-access network. Information can change where people go, but it cannot create road throughput or shelter capacity that the physical system does not have.

9
00:01:57,050 --> 00:02:10,013
Noto is the stress case. Sparse settlement, limited network redundancy, and constrained destinations reveal why better guidance may help early yet concentrate demand and harm later outcomes.

10
00:02:10,563 --> 00:02:29,073
Kumamoto is added as a dedicated magnitude seven point one scenario. It uses nineteen thousand eight hundred fifty-seven road-enclosed blocks, five hundred ninety-three official earthquake shelters, sampled agent routes, and a population-conserving one hundred eighty minute history.

11
00:02:29,623 --> 00:02:41,536
Kathmandu completes the seven-city overseas set. Reusing the same evidence interface helps separate differences caused by urban form and capacity from differences caused by presentation.

12
00:02:42,086 --> 00:02:57,717
Local language-model inference is verified on AMD Radeon through ROCm with measured runtime, throughput, validity, concurrency, and memory evidence. Decisions are constrained, logged, and applied back into the simulation.

13
00:02:58,267 --> 00:03:15,648
The research contribution is an auditable scenario laboratory linking individual behavior, physical capacity, information, and city-scale outcomes. It supports privacy-preserving counterfactual analysis, but it is not a forecast or an official evacuation plan.

14
00:03:16,198 --> 00:03:32,520
We gratefully acknowledge AMD for cloud computing resources that supported large-scale data preparation, multi-city simulation, rendering, and validation. This acknowledgment does not imply AMD endorsement of the methods or conclusions.
